# Cloudflare applies every rule that matches a path and joins repeated headers
# with a comma. Left to itself the build generates overlapping rules: /_nuxt/*
# (cache for a year) also matches /_nuxt/builds/*, so latest.json went out as
#   cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable, public, max-age=1, immutable
# and a browser that honours the first value never notices a new deploy.
#
# This file replaces the generated one. Nitro skips its own rules when it finds
# a line that starts with "/* " (slash, star, space), so the trailing space on
# the first rule below is load-bearing. Keep it.
#
# Order matters too: broad rules first, then the narrower ones detach the
# inherited header (the leading "!") before setting their own.
/* 
  x-content-type-options: nosniff
/_nuxt/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/_fonts/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/_scripts/assets/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/_nuxt/builds/*
  ! cache-control
  cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/_nuxt/builds/meta/*
  ! cache-control
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
